IMPORT prelude

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1954 (Qld), Part 10 -- Service of documents (ss 39 and 39A).
-- When service by post is taken to have been effected (s 39A(1)(b)) is in qld-interpretation-time.l4.

§ `Part 10 -- Service of documents`

§§ `s 39 -- Service of documents`

DECLARE `Person served` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

DECLARE `Way of serving a document` IS ONE OF
    `by delivering it to the person personally`
    `by leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document`
    `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document`
    `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate`
    `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate`
    `in any other way`

-- (1): the document "may be served" in the stated ways.  A permission; another way is not answered by this subsection (see (3)): NOTHING.
-- src:839 | (1) If an Act requires or permits a document to be served on a person, the document may be served—
-- src:840 | (a) on an individual—
-- src:841 | (i) by delivering it to the person personally; or
-- src:842 | (ii) by leaving it at, or by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to, the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document; or
-- src:843 | (b) on a body corporate—by leaving it at, or sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to, the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate.
@ref s 39(1) (src:839-843)
GIVEN `an Act requires or permits a document to be served on a person` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `Person served`
      way IS A `Way of serving a document`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document may be served in the way (s 39(1))` IS
    IF NOT `an Act requires or permits a document to be served on a person`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER person
        WHEN `an individual` THEN
            CONSIDER way
            WHEN `by delivering it to the person personally` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `by leaving it at the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the address of the place of residence or business of the person last known to the person serving the document` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING
        WHEN `a body corporate` THEN
            CONSIDER way
            WHEN `by leaving it at the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `by sending it by post, telex, facsimile or similar facility to the head office, a registered office or a principal office of the body corporate` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING

DECLARE `Expression used for serving` IS ONE OF
    deliver
    give
    notify
    send
    serve
    `another expression`

-- src:844 | (2) Subsection (1) applies whether the expression ‘deliver’, ‘give’, ‘notify’, ‘send’ or ‘serve’ or another expression is used.
@ref s 39(2) (src:844-844)
GIVEN expression IS AN `Expression used for serving`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsection (1) applies whichever expression is used (s 39(2))` IS JUST TRUE

-- src:845 | (3) Nothing in subsection (1)—
-- src:846 | (a) affects the operation of another law that authorises the service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection; or
@ref s 39(3) (src:845-846)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1) affects the operation of another law that authorises the service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection (s 39(3)(a))` IS FALSE

-- src:847 | (b) affects the power of a court or tribunal to authorise service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection.
@ref s 39(3) (src:847-847)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 39(1) affects the power of a court or tribunal to authorise service of a document otherwise than as provided in the subsection (s 39(3)(b))` IS FALSE

§§ `s 39A -- Meaning of service by post etc.`

-- src:849 | (1) If an Act requires or permits a document to be served by post, service—
-- src:850 | (a) may be effected by properly addressing, prepaying and posting the document as a letter; and
@ref s 39A(1) (src:849-850)
GIVEN `the document is properly addressed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is prepaid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is posted as a letter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `service by post may be effected (s 39A(1)(a))` IS
    IF `the document is properly addressed` AND `the document is prepaid` AND `the document is posted as a letter` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING

-- src:852 | (2) If an Act requires or permits a document to be served by a particular postal method, the requirement or permission is taken to be satisfied if the document is posted by that method or, if that method is not available, by the equivalent, or nearest equivalent, method provided for the time being by Australia Post.
@ref s 39A(2) (src:852-852)
GIVEN `the document is posted by the particular postal method` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that method is not available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document is posted by the equivalent, or nearest equivalent, method provided for the time being by Australia Post` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requirement or permission to serve by a particular postal method is taken to be satisfied (s 39A(2))` IS
    IF `the document is posted by the particular postal method` OR (`that method is not available` AND `the document is posted by the equivalent, or nearest equivalent, method provided for the time being by Australia Post`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- src:853 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) apply whether the expression ‘deliver’, ‘give’, ‘notify’, ‘send’ or ‘serve’ or another expression is used.
@ref s 39A(3) (src:853-853)
GIVEN expression IS AN `Expression used for serving`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subsections (1) and (2) apply whichever expression is used (s 39A(3))` IS JUST TRUE
